# Harness `just ci` runs only scripts/tests/{harness,invariants,adr-lint}.test.mjs and lints only
# scripts/ — so for a slice touching solely memory/projects/** it CANNOT fail. Gating a harness
# slice on it would be a green light that means nothing, which is the defect class lp-00 removes.
repo_block=("REPO: **harness** (`mdrewt/claude-harness`). Worktree from `origin/main`; PR on the harness repo.\n"
 "GATE — read this, it is not the project gate: harness `just ci` runs only `scripts/tests/*` and lints only `scripts/`, so for a slice touching solely `memory/projects/**` it **cannot fail** and proves nothing. Your gate is **`memory/projects/mr-selfcheck` printing SELFCHECK-OK** plus **the `--selftest` of every tool you touched or added**. mr-selfcheck DERIVES its tool set (lp-00), so a new executable `mr-*` is picked up automatically — but it must carry a bash or python shebang or the gate fails it as unclassifiable, and anything with real logic should ship a `--selftest` wired in beside mr-cost-sum's. Run harness `just ci` too (cheap, catches script-lint regressions), but never report it as the gate.\n"
 "There is no remote CI on this repo and no branch protection, so 'PR open + local gate green' IS the terminal state; the supervisor merges.\n"
 if repo=="harness" else
 "REPO: **project** (`mdrewt/monster-realm`). Worktree from `origin/master`; PR on the project repo.\n"
 "GATE: the full `just ci` (the exact gate remote runs — incl. Semgrep/security) green locally before opening the PR.\n")
# lp-skills: fail LOUD if the template lost the anchor. Silently rendering a brief with no
# skills block is the invisible under-fire this slice exists to remove.
if "<SKILLS_BLOCK>" not in tpl:
    raise SystemExit("brief template is missing the <SKILLS_BLOCK> placeholder: %s" % sys.argv[1])
_subbed=[]
for k,val in [("<SLICE>",v["slice"]),("<ADR_NUM>",str(v.get("adr",""))),("<TOUCHES>",touches_str),
              ("<TARGET_DESC>",str(v.get("target_desc",""))),("<RESUME_BLOCK>",str(rb)),("<TIER_BLOCK>",tier_block),
              ("<REPO_BLOCK>",repo_block),("<PR_REPO>",os.environ["PR_REPO"]),
              ("<BASE_BRANCH>",os.environ["BASE_BRANCH"]),("<WT_ROOT>",os.environ["WT_ROOT"]),
              ("<CAP_USD>",str(__import__("os").environ.get("CAP","60"))),
              ("<SKILLS_BLOCK>",sys.argv[3])]:
    _subbed.append(k)
    tpl=tpl.replace(k,val)
# Keyed to the list JUST iterated, so a renamed placeholder cannot drift out of the check, and
# scoped to template segments so caller content never trips it. Post-F1 this is a POST-CONDITION
# on the segment machinery rather than a template-drift detector (a template segment cannot
# survive its own key); it bites if _Doc.replace ever regresses. Genuine template drift is caught
# by the pre-loop <SKILLS_BLOCK> assert above.
_left=[k for k in _subbed if k in tpl]
if _left:
    raise SystemExit("unsubstituted placeholder(s) survived rendering: %s" % _left)
rendered=str(tpl)
open(sys.argv[2],"w").write(rendered)
print("brief-built bytes=%d tier=%s repo=%s" % (len(rendered),tier,repo))
PYBRIEF
  rc=$?
  if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then
    brief_notice BRIEF-RENDER-FAILED "rendering $tpl -> $out failed (rc=$rc); most likely the template lost a placeholder the renderer requires. Refusing — a partially-substituted brief must never launch."
